The embedding problem","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:911fa6426b66237b3ce16ee90bc4c5bb3900e10467708ae9ce7688c727914b0a","file":"preprints/An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":36,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"c9d5c388bbd8a5f7156293646a2c88dd4b8248e71b9737e7d2968477056ece5c","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:911fa6426b66237b3ce16ee90bc4c5bb3900e10467708ae9ce7688c727914b0a","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026/build/introduction.tex#L36"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet\n\\[\n G=\\Z[1/2]^3\\rtimes\\bigl(\\SL_3(\\Z)\\times\\Z\\bigr),\n \\qquad (M,k)\\cdot v=2^kMv,\n\\]\nand let $A=C^*(G)$ be its full group $C^*$-algebra. Then $A$ is separable\nand unital. For every nonzero unital nuclear $C^*$-algebra $B$ and every\nfree ultrafilter $\\omega$ on $\\N$, there is no unital embedding\n\\[\n A\\longrightarrow B^\\omega.\n\\]\nIn particular, $A$ does not embed unitally into $\\Otwo^\\omega$."},{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:50e177434bc0b05da9947ee5c7190cb49d9fcc53c9edc237748546fc5ccbc506","grain":"paper-statement","id":"An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026#cor:kep-consequences","title":"Consequences of negative KEP"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry"